# Security rules

- Secrets ONLY in `.env.local` (gitignored), generated by `scripts/sync-env.sh`.
  Never print, log, or commit a secret value; never echo env values into the client
  bundle (no `NEXT_PUBLIC_` for anything sensitive).
- Owner-only auth: login page is the only unauthenticated route. Session cookie:
  HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax, 30-day rolling. Rate-limit login (5 fails/15min).
  No registration endpoint exists.
- CSRF: all mutating API routes require same-origin + session; webhook/trigger routes
  use their own signed tokens instead.
- The LHOS approvals page token (`APPROVE_TOKEN`) is **human-only**: the panel may
  link to LHOS approvals/read `GET /api/approvals`, and may proxy approve/reject only
  behind the owner's authenticated session — never expose the token to any model or
  client code, and never let the agent loop call approve/reject.
- File uploads: size-capped, extension-allowlisted, stored outside web root, served
  via authenticated route. Images passed to vision models are re-encoded.
- Vendor/webhook/connector keys entered in Settings are stored encrypted at rest
  (AES-256-GCM, key = env `PANEL_SECRET_KEY`) in the `secrets` table; UI shows
  last-4 only; there is no "reveal" endpoint.
- Dependencies: no abandoned packages; pin majors; `npm audit` before release.
- This platform automates the owner's OWN accounts within each platform's ToS.
  Do not implement anti-bot-detection, fingerprint spoofing, or evasion features;
  pacing = plain rate limiting via LHOS `set_pace` only.
